{
  "_why": "Coverage audit 2026-10-05 (owner: 'I want to see ALL changes to everything in the game'): 2,040 gameplay changes (1,340 not in the patch notes) were on no hero, item or unit page — the Soul Urn rework of 2026-06-04, crates, powerups, the Rejuvenator, soul sharing, the level curve, respawn times and soul rewards (console variables). They are the Game section (builders/game_systems.py): a system is a page like a unit family's, its parts are groups of entries. Every rule is a regex tried from the start of a subject, systems and parts in this order, the first match wins. Subjects: an entry 'file:id#kind' ('misc.vdata:citadel_breakable_item_container#global'), a row of a rule for every hero or ability 'file:@all:path' ('heroes.vdata:@all:m_mapLevelInfo.10…'), a console variable 'convar:name'. Whatever no system names falls to 'other' (nothing is lost); a console variable only shows when a part names it (UI, bots and debug switches stay in the patch archive). Names: the game's files give most of these entries no text, so the site names them here (never their ids); icons come from the game files (icons/…) or the site's pixel glyphs ('glyph:…'), never invented art.",
  "_why_display": "The order the pages list the systems in (the 'systems' order below is the regexes' precedence: the Urn's soul orbs before every soul orb).",
  "display": ["souls", "respawn", "progression", "urn", "pickups", "breakables", "troopers", "camps", "shop", "combat", "modes", "other"],
