  "_why_convars": "Console variables show only when a part names them, the game server reads them ('gamedll' in their flags) and their name is no test or display switch (`hide`): crate respawn times are flagged 'cheat' and are the real values, so flags alone cannot tell. The first build with console variables (6395, 2026-03-10) is where tracking starts: its 1,365 entries are a snapshot, not changes.",
  "convar_hide": "(debug|_log|log_|bot_|_bot|test|_wip|wip_|experiment|cache|query|validate|audit|anim|nav|hitbox|motor|glow|celebration|visibility|_text|offset|status|stuck|waypoint|think|per_tick|tick_limit|hero_demo|release_vote|forced_hero|model|observer|stateful|pipeline|use_new|_v2|override)",
  "_why_units": "A console variable's unit from its snake_case name (AGENTS rule 6: numbers as the game shows them — metres = engine units / 39.37, seconds and percents with their unit; Game rules read 'citadel_bounty_aoe_radius 2165.35', review 2026-10-05). [regex, unit, scale]: the first match wins; scale 'units' divides engine units by 39.37, 'x100' turns a 0..1 fraction into a percent, '' keeps the number. A name that says '_meters' is metres already; '_time' alone is not a unit (the trooper waves' '_late_time 20' counts minutes, the reward's '_time 2400' seconds), nor 'ratio' or 'percent' (0.005 or 1.5). No match = a bare number.",
  "convar_units": [
    ["(multiplier|_mult|_scale|ratio|percent)", "", ""],
    ["_meters?$", "m", ""],
    ["fraction$", "%", "x100"],
    ["(_pct$|_pct_)", "%", ""],
    ["(radius|range|distance|thickness|width|spacing|padding)(_[a-z_]+)?$", "m", "units"],
    ["(movespeed_bonus_max|leap_speed|force_speed)$", "m/s", "units"],
    ["(_duration|_duration_s|_interval|_delay|_window|_extratime|duration_until_decay|warning_time|notification_time|aggro_time|sleep_time|reward_time|spawn_time_base|spawn_time_variance|spawn_time_(max|min)_ramp_[0-9]|max_respawn_time|in_base_penalty|_ramp_[0-9]_time|ramp_gametime|tick_gold_start_time)$", "s", ""]
  ],
  "_why_polarity": "A console variable's side for whoever takes it, from its snake_case name (the vdata polarity rules read CamelCase fields): more souls is better for the taker, a shorter respawn or spawn timer too (semantics.PLAYER_SIDE); a ramp's time, comeback scales and warnings have no side (UP / DOWN). First match wins; no match = no side.",
  "convar_polarity": [
    ["spawn_time_[a-z0-9_]*_time$", 0],
    ["(spawn_time|death_return_to_spawn)", -1],
    ["(comeback|difficulty|redirect|ratio|fraction)", 0],
    ["(gold_reward|gold_drop|reward_base|reward_time_multiplier|bounty|gold_amount|reward_buff_count|buff_count|orbs_to_spawn)", 1],
    ["(respawn_interval|spawn_initial_delay|initial_delay)", -1]
  ],
